          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أطاع (aṭāʿa) is built on the native Arabic root ṭ-w-ʿ, \"to comply, to be willing\" (Lane). Istaṭāʿa, to be able, which you know, is from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
